course: dictionary
lesson: 10027
title: A word from Madagascar
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tenrec is a small mammal, which means an animal with fur that feeds its babies milk. Tenrecs live on the island of Madagascar, off the coast of Africa, and many of them look like hedgehogs or shrews.
explain: «Tenrecs look like hedgehogs or shrews but are actually related to elephants and aardvarks, African animals that dig for ants.» The word but is your clue. It tells you the first idea, that a tenrec is like a hedgehog, is only part of the story.
explain: Some tenrecs have spines, which are sharp prickles like a hedgehog's. Others do not. When you read about an animal, look for words that tell you how it looks, and check whether the sentence says "some" or "all".
fact: A tenrec is a small mammal from Madagascar.
fact: Some tenrecs have spines, which are sharp prickles.
fact: Tenrecs can look like hedgehogs but are not closely related to them.
fact: Some tenrecs rattle their quills to talk to each other.
fact: Some tenrecs have many babies at once.
exercise: What is a tenrec? | A plant with sharp leaves | *A small mammal from Madagascar that often looks like a hedgehog | A huge bird that cannot fly | A fish that lives in rivers
exercise: «Some shrews and tenrecs use simple echoes from squeaks to explore tunnels and thick grass.» Which animal does a tenrec often look like? | A whale | A cat | A horse | *A hedgehog
exercise: «Some tenrecs have spines.» What are spines? | Shiny scales | Soft feathers | *Sharp prickles | Big floppy ears
test: «Tenrecs look like hedgehogs or shrews but are actually related to elephants and aardvarks.» What does the word but tell you? | The animal is a hedgehog after all | Tenrecs and elephants are the same size | *The first idea is only part of the story | The sentence is finished
test: Where do tenrecs live? | In the Arctic snow | In the middle of the Sahara desert | *On the island of Madagascar | At the bottom of the sea
exam: «Some shrews and tenrecs use simple echoes from squeaks to explore tunnels and thick grass.» What does a tenrec use squeaks for? | To cook food | *To explore tunnels and thick grass | To fly over the sea | To change colour
